<title>CANADA: Forest Oil converts Saxon pfds.</title>
<headline>Forest Oil converts Saxon pfds.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saxon Petroleum Inc said on Wednesday that Forest Oil Corp elected to convert the 15,500,000 series A preferred shares of Saxon that it held into 27,192,983 non-voting shares, effective today.</p>
<p>Saxon said after conversion of the preferred shares, Forest would own about 82 million common and non-voting shares of Saxon. Forest's ownership is 48 percent of the common shares, 65 percent of total issued shares and on a fully diluted basis, 100 million shares or 65 percent.</p>
<p>Saxon chief executive Glen Tarrant said the conversion simplified Saxon's capital structure and relieved Saxon of a C$620,000 a year dividend requirement. Saxon's debt-free capital structure consists of common and non-voting shares.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
